# piactl WITHOUT a timeout hangs the login: when pia-daemon is wedged (it was, for
# 34 days, Aug-Sep 2026) every call blocks for ~5s and any SSH session becomes slow
# exactly when you need to get in and debug. See systemd/PIA.md.
pia() { timeout 5 piactl "$@" 2>/dev/null; }

#PIA — the region is NOT hardcoded: a re-added token can return a different IP
#      (Sep 2026: .86 -> .79), and a fixed id then becomes "Unknown region".
#piactl dedicatedip add ~/piatoken.txt
#piactl set region "$(piactl get regions | grep -m1 '^dedicated-')"
#piactl set requestportforward true
#piactl connect
#

# `pubip` is the PHYSICAL link's IP (the ISP line) and stays on it even when the
# tunnel is perfectly healthy — shown on its own it looked like the server was
# leaving unprotected. What matters for the Binance key whitelist is `vpnip`.
printf "🔐 VPN State      : %s\n" "$(pia get connectionstate)"
printf "🔌 Port Forward   : %s\n" "$(pia get portforward)"
printf "🌍 VPN exit IP    : %s\n" "$(pia get vpnip)"
printf "🏠 ISP link IP    : %s\n" "$(pia get pubip)"

